.SH "NAME"
radeontop \- report Radeon GPU utilization
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
\fBradeontop [\-cThmv] [\-\-dither\-seed \fR\fB\fIseed\fR\fR\fB] [\-b \fR\fB\fIbus\fR\fR\fB] [\-d \fR\fB\fIfile\fR\fR\fB] [\-i \fR\fB\fIseconds\fR\fR\fB] [\-l \fR\fB\fIlimit\fR\fR\fB] [\-p \fR\fB\fIdevice\fR\fR\fB] [\-t \fR\fB\fIticks\fR\fR\fB]\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
RadeonTop samples Radeon engine\-status registers and reports total GPU activity plus the hardware blocks whose status bits have an exposed gauge\&.
.sp
R600 and later use GRBM_STATUS through a radeon or amdgpu DRM interface when available\&. R300\-class integrated graphics (RS400, RS480, RS482, and RS485) use RBBM_STATUS through PCI resource2; detection selects the direct path when the radeon read\-register ioctl rejects the pre\-R600 register\&.
.sp
Every dump invocation emits one radeontop_capture_v1 JSON header\&. It carries one clean source commit, the exact source and build manifests plus their digests, boot and device identity, and the byte\-escaped command vector\&. Dump mode rejects dirty and unknown source identities because they lack an immutable source object\&. Each data line retains its human\-readable fields and ends with an evidence_v1 JSON object containing the run identity, timing, slot accounting, capability and signal state, clock means, lane denominators, and unconditional missing\-data bounds\&. A radeontop_run_end_v1 footer records the logical exit reason and final collector state\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\fB\-b, \-\-bus \fR\fB\fIbus\fR\fR
.RS 4
Select one hexadecimal PCI bus number from 00 through ff\&. For the lspci address
01:00\&.0, the bus argument is
1\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-c, \-\-color\fR
.RS 4
Enable colorized output\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-d, \-\-dump \fR\fB\fIfile\fR\fR
.RS 4
Append dump records to
\fIfile\fR\&. An argument equal to
\-
writes stdout; other names, including names beginning with
\-, name regular files\&. Each invocation appends a new provenance header\&. A regular destination, including redirected stdout, carries an exclusive lock for the whole run\&. A nonempty regular destination receives a newline record boundary before the new header, so a truncated prior record cannot absorb the run identity\&. Runtime diagnostics use stderr\&.
SIGTERM
and
SIGINT
request an orderly footer, flush, and shutdown\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-dither\-seed \fR\fB\fIseed\fR\fR
.RS 4
Offset each sample reproducibly inside its own exact slot using a nonzero seed from 1 through 4294967295\&. Rejection sampling gives every nanosecond in the slot equal probability\&. Omitting the option keeps samples on the exact deadline grid\&. Dithering breaks fixed workload\-phase lock, while scheduler lateness can reduce accepted coverage near the end of a slot\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Display help on stdout and exit successfully\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-i, \-\-dump\-interval \fR\fB\fIseconds\fR\fR
.RS 4
Publish one dump window every
\fIseconds\fR\&. The accepted range is 1 through 86400 and the default is 1\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-l, \-\-limit \fR\fB\fIlimit\fR\fR
.RS 4
Stop after
\fIlimit\fR
data lines in dump mode\&. Zero, the default, runs until termination\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-m, \-\-mem\fR
.RS 4
Force the direct PCI sysfs
resourceN
MMIO path selected by the known device family\&. An unknown PCI ID has no admitted direct layout\&. With \-\-path, this option forces MMIO for the same selected PCI device\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-p, \-\-path \fR\fB\fIdevice\fR\fR
.RS 4
Open the named DRM device node and derive its exact PCI identity\&. The path selects the device instead of \-\-bus; \-\-mem can still force the validated direct status path for that same device\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-t, \-\-ticks \fR\fB\fIticks\fR\fR
.RS 4
Request
\fIticks\fR
samples per second from 1 through 1000000\&. The default rate is 120\&. A higher rate increases temporal resolution and overhead; scheduler lateness and register\-read cost can reduce the valid sample count\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-T, \-\-transparency\fR
.RS 4
Enable terminal transparency\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-v, \-\-version\fR
.RS 4
Display the source version and exit successfully\&.
.RE
.SH "INTERACTIVE COMMANDS"
.PP
\fBC, c\fR
.RS 4
Toggle colorized output\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBQ, q\fR
.RS 4
Quit\&.
.RE
